  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "10"
  ],
  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the amount of Hanna's food order was&nbsp;<math alttext=\"dollar sign 50\"><mo>$</mo><mn>50</mn></math> and that Hanna gave a tip of <math alttext=\"20 percent sign\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the amount of the bill.&nbsp;<math alttext=\"20 percent sign\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math> can be calculated as <math alttext=\"left parenthesis StartFraction 20 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis left parenthesis 50 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mn>50</mn></mfenced></math>, which yields <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1000 Over 100 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>1000</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, the amount, in dollars, of the tip Hanna gave is <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math>.</p>",
